# fixedbugs, defect 559, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's R1), the shape
# beside the repair.
#
# A module's unit reads its own groups' headers since defect 559, and no
# other module's: until then every unit read every group record's header.
# A unit that spells another module's group record still reads that
# record's header, since the record's C type is the header's: this module
# builds one into an array and compares it, and `holder` passes it, holds
# it in a record of its own and reads its fields, each unit including
# `fixedbugs-559-points.h`, and only `holder`'s its own header beside it.
use fixedbugs559/holder
use fixedbugs559/points

function main()
    p = points.make(v: 3)
    print(holder.get(p: p))
    h = holder.hold(p: p)
    xs = [p, points.make(v: 1)]
    print(xs.len())
    print(h.p.w)
    print(p == xs[0])
